OL,3,GNEWSAValve failure on CalMac ferry saw
OL,4,Auncontrolled escape of flammable gas
OL,5,
OL,6,FA faulty valve on a CalMac ferry led to
OL,7,Fa sudden and uncontrolled release of
OL,8,Fhighly flammable methane gas last
OL,9,Fsummer, BBC Scotland News has learned.
OL,11,FThe operator's investigation found that
OL,12,F700kg of the gas - enough to fill a
OL,13,Ffour-bedroomed house - was vented from
OL,14,Fthe side of MV Glen Sannox over the
OL,15,Fspace of 12 minutes while it was
OL,16,Fcarrying 82 passengers from Arran to
OL,17,Fthe mainland.
OL,19,FSo much methane was released that some
OL,20,Fof it was sucked into a ventilation
OL,21,Fintake, setting off gas alarms in the
OL,22,Fship's generator room.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,429,420,260,160,0,100
